== 3. THE THREE mtime BLOCKERS, RE-TESTED AGAINST A CONTENT SHA ==
  (1) differ.py:58-60 refuses a `git` dependency ON PURPOSE.
      `git` on PATH here: True; the digest path imports only
      ['hashlib', 'os', 'pathlib']. It calls no subprocess and reads no ref, so
      the dependency `differ.py` declines is one this row never takes.  NOT HIT.
  (2) runs/ is gitignored, so an mtime is a fact about THIS TREE.
      clone A digest : 72f4b3f9eac6b905   clone B digest : 72f4b3f9eac6b905   -> AGREE
      after rewriting every mtime of B (now 3 distinct values, spread 4000000000000 ns): 72f4b3f9eac6b905 -> UNCHANGED
      an mtime rule would have had to compare those 3 numbers; a content sha
      never reads one.  NOT HIT.
  (3) writing two rows moves consumers it does not own.
      live summary rows 22, keys ['byte-identical', 'census-rc', 'conflations', 'controls', 'cross', 'dev', 'expect-moved', 'graphs', 'graphs-agree', 'graphs-answered', 'graphs-disagree', 'graphs-unset', 'lc_all', 'noopt', 'not-comparable', 'oracle-selfcheck', 'plants-disagree', 'pythonhashseed', 'selfcheck', 'stable-differ', 'stable-failed', 'stable-pairs']
      'substrate-start' is inside the PINS table, so unhealthy() would JUDGE it: False
      'substrate-end' is inside the PINS table, so unhealthy() would JUDGE it: False
      `unhealthy()` judges `k in PINS` only, so a key outside PINS is INVISIBLE to it:
      that is WHY these two rows must NOT be pinned -- a pin on a substrate digest would
      have to be re-pinned every time the port moves, which is `pinindep`'s finding that
      17 pins on one file is one measurement wearing 17 hats, made worse.
      unhealthy() on the PADDED summary : 0 complaint(s), unchanged from the unpadded 0  -> True
      checks/disagree-gate.py      parses it by: summary = (tree / "D0-run-summary.txt").read_text().splitlines()
      checks/corpus-figure.py      parses it by: # from its own output cannot fail either").  MEASURED: `runs/graphcmp/D/D0-run
      NOT HIT, and only because the rows are additive keys outside PINS.

